<h4 id="the-ideal-lens">The ideal lens</h4>

<p>The ideal lens is a mathematical abstraction which provides perfect imaging given by a projective transformation between the object and image space.</p>

<p>The constants appearing in this transformation specify the positions of the cardinal planes of the lens. The six important cardinal planes are the two focus planes, the two principal planes, and the two nodal planes.</p>

